<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE electron-strix14-2026-11-27 ascent</name><description>FLOWN 2026-11-27. T0 is the actual liftoff 2026-11-27T00:15:00Z (+900 s from the pre-flight window open 2026-11-27T00:00:00Z). LL2 id 2093e4fc-ac8c-4296-a1b5-deececee6a72 is Launch Successful, net 2026-11-27T00:15:00Z, minute precision, last_updated 2026-11-27T04:48:55Z. Rocket Lab mission page: 1:15 p.m. NZDT, 101st launch overall. Rocket Lab mission-success post (dateline 27 November 2026): the StriX satellite was delivered to a 569 km orbit; 22nd launch of 2026 and 101st mission overall. That post writes 27 September 2026 once; September was not used. UTC columns and KML &lt;when&gt; tags shifted +900 s. Elapsed times and ECEF geometry unchanged. Sim not re-run. ILLUSTRATIVE.
ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Electron &#x27;Night Owls Never Sleep&#x27; (StriX Launch 14) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
PRE-FLIGHT. Not telemetry. Single Synspective StriX SAR satellite, Rocket Lab LC-1, Mahia.
T0 is the Rocket Lab mission-page window open 2026-11-27T00:00:00Z (NET 1:00 p.m. NZDT 27 Nov; Thu 26 Nov 4:00 p.m. PST). https://rocketlabcorp.com/missions/launches/night-owls-never-sleep/
SOURCE CONFLICT, not silent. The mission page pairs 1:00 p.m. NZDT with UTC 00:00. The launch-safety page prints &#x27;NET 00:05 UTC | 13:00 NZDT&#x27; (https://rocketlabcorp.com/launch/launch-safety/); 13:00 NZDT is 00:00Z, so those two clocks on that page disagree, and 00:05Z is not 13:00 NZDT. LL2 id 2093e4fc-ac8c-4296-a1b5-deececee6a72 is Go, NET 2026-11-27T00:05:00Z, window 00:00-00:05Z, minute precision, last_updated 2026-11-20T06:34:05Z. T0 is the mission-page 00:00Z. The 00:05Z figures were not used.
Loft: Rocket Lab Electron Payload User Guide 8.0 GENERIC example flight profile (not this mission): altitude knots 0@0s, ~78km@155s (S1 cutoff), ~82km@162s (S2 ignition), ~126km@184s (fairing sep); S2 cutoff L+535s. https://rocketlabcorp.com/assets/Rocket-Lab-Electron-Payload-User-Guide-8.0.pdf
Rocket Lab has published NO flight timeline for Night Owls Never Sleep. The mission page gives 569 km LEO and inclination 38 deg, and no deploy time.
Assumptions: (a) S2-cutoff altitude set to the published 569 km orbit, altitude linear 184s-&gt;535s; (b) ground-relative horizontal speed ramps linearly 0 -&gt; 7.218 km/s (circular v at 569 km minus Earth rotation along Az) at 535s.
Real Electron parks in a lower elliptical orbit and the Kick Stage circularizes later (timing unpublished); this file ends at S2 cutoff.
Azimuth 81.97 deg: mean great-circle bearing from LC-1 to the vertex-average centroids of NAVAREA XIV 338/26 space-debris areas. Area A centroid 38.1500S 175.0625W, bearing 80.85 deg, 626 km. Area B centroid 35.8250S 163.1250W, bearing 83.10 deg, 1716 km. Daily 1615-0130Z, 26 Nov-10 Dec 2026, which covers 00:00Z on 27 Nov. https://www.sealagom.com/navarea/14/message/26090/338-26-area-bounded/ The near-field marine box (NZ Coastal 306/26, also on the launch-safety page, ~25 km from the pad) was not used.
Non-rotating inclination from 81.97 deg is 39.94 deg. Rocket Lab publishes 38 deg. That figure is 1.26 deg below the pad latitude (39.26S): sin(az)=cos(38)/cos(39.260881) is 1.018, so 38 deg is not a non-rotating heading from Mahia. The hazard azimuth was not retuned toward it.
Payload: 1x StriX (StriX Launch 14), Synspective 100 kg class (https://www.synspective.com/satellite/satellite-strix/). The 100 kg is a class, not a weighed Launch 14 mass.
Pad (LL2, this launch): -39.260881N 177.865826E. Elevation ASSUMED 0 m. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s.
Constant-azimuth rhumb Az=81.97 deg from pad, spherical R=6371.0088 km. Velocity ECEF: v_horiz along Az + hdot Up in local ENU.
T0 used: 2026-11-27T00:15:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
